Name: MC_POLDIJETS
Summary: Loose polarized dijet observables for parton-shower spin comparisons at 510 GeV
Status: UNVALIDATED
Reentrant: true
Authors:
  - Andreas Papaefstathiou <apapaefs@kennesaw.edu>
References:
RunInfo: Requires independent PP, PM, MP, and MM polarized pp samples.
NumEvents: 100000
NeedsCrossSection: yes
Beams: [p+, p+]
Energies: [510]
Options:
 - LEVEL=HARDPARTON,HADRON
 - R=#
 - PTJ1MIN=#
 - PTJ2MIN=#
 - PTJ3MIN=#
 - PTJ4MIN=#
 - ETAMAX=#
Description: >
  An MC_JETS-inspired analysis for comparing spin-correlated and
  spin-averaged parton showers with the polarized hard process unchanged.
  The default hard-shower-parton selection uses anti-kT R=0.5,
  pT1>5 GeV, pT2>4 GeV, and |eta|<1.5, without topology, Delta-phi, or
  Delta-eta cuts. The campaign postprocessor constructs sigma_UU,
  Delta sigma_LL, A_LL, helicity-resolved cross sections, and single-spin/
  parity closure observables from independent PP, PM, MP, and MM samples.
